course: dictionary
lesson: 15566
title: Surrounded: all around you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Surround means to be all around something. Surrounded is the past form, so it tells us about something that already happened: «The island was surrounded by water.» Picture the island with water on every side.
explain: Surrounded is also used as an adjective with by, as in «surrounded by». Being surrounded by something means having it all around you. «I grew up surrounded by animals» means animals were all around me when I was growing up.
explain: Look for the clue word by. The thing after by is what is all around. «The castle was surrounded by a deep moat» tells you the moat was on every side of the castle.
fact: Surround means to be all around something.
fact: Surrounded is the past of surround: was or were all around something.
fact: As an adjective, «surrounded by» means having things or people all around you.
fact: «The players surrounded the referee.» They stood all around him.
fact: Surrounded can also describe a shape with a border all around it.
exercise: «The island was surrounded by water.» What does surrounded mean here? | Had a big bridge across it | *Had water all around it | Was dry and sandy all over | Was hidden under a cloud
exercise: «The castle was surrounded by a deep moat.» Where was the moat? | *All around the castle | Inside the tower | Under the castle only | Far away over the hills
exercise: Find and copy the past form of surround in this sentence: «The lost dog was surrounded by children.» | dog | lost | children | *surrounded
test: «I grew up surrounded by animals.» What does surrounded by mean? | *Having animals all around me | Feeding animals once a week | Afraid of animals | Far away from animals
test: Ben says, «The park is surrounded by houses.» What does he mean? | The park is made of houses | The park is far from houses | *Houses stand all around the park | Houses are inside the park
exam: In «The ship was surrounded by ice», which word is the past form of surround? | by | ice | ship | *surrounded
